# BUGS

No Kit app is scriptable: actions are invoked by controls, keys and menus only.
The accessibility tree is built each frame but not given to Radharc, which has no readers; there are no secure windows.
Shifted characters come from kbdfs's built-in US map, not from a map loaded into kbdfs.
Keys don't repeat, and the pointer leaving a window isn't heard, so the control last under it stays hot.
Every face in `/lib/fonts` is read whole, once, at a session's start, those its theme doesn't name too.
A frame's allocations are not counted on the device.
Kit's views neither start nor take drags: a Kit app hears none of the SDK's drag events.
